 meeting","description":"For the second time this year, the SEC is threatening to hold a vote of its chancellors and presidents on whether to kick LSU out of the league, according to a filing in federal court in Alabama on Monday.","published":"2026-11-24T01:38:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/50577602/sec-consider-termination-lsu-membership","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia defensive coordinator Glenn Schumann agrees to coach Florida State","description":"Georgia's Glenn Schumann, one of the country's top defensive coordinators and part of a staff that has the Bulldogs at No. 1 in the CFP rankings, agreed to a five-year deal to become the next coach at Florida State, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-24T00:49:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577665/uga-defensive-coordinator-schumann-coach-florida-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Aiden Flora, nation's leading rusher, re-signs with Iowa State for next season","description":"Iowa State running back Aiden Flora, who leads the nation in rushing, announced Monday that he has re-signed with the Cyclones for next season.","published":"2026-11-23T23:57:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577520/aiden-flora-nation-leading-rusher-re-signs-iowa-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas A&M names John Thornton interim athletic director effective Dec. 1","description":"John Thornton will take over as interim athletic director at Texas A&M, effective Dec. 1, replacing the departed Trev Alberts.","published":"2026-11-23T22:07:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50576559/texas-names-john-thornton-interim-ad-effective-dec-1","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Giants DC Dennard Wilson interviews for HC job at alma mater Maryland","description":"Giants defensive coordinator Dennard Wilson had a virtual interview recently for the vacant head coaching job at Maryland, sources told NFL Network.","published":"2026-11-23T21:22:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50575838/sources-giants-dennard-wilson-interviews-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU's Lane Kiffin apologizes for using profanity during halftime interview","description":"LSU coach Lane Kiffin has apologized for using profanity during a halftime interview with the school's radio network in Saturday's loss to Tennessee.","published":"2026-11-23T20:12:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575735/lsu-kiffin-apologizes-use-profanity-interview","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest leading rusher Ty Clark ruled out for season","description":"Wake Forest running back Ty Clark will miss the rest of the season, coach Jake Dickert announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T20:30:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575731/wake-forest-leading-rusher-ry-clark-ruled-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Syracuse rules QB Steve Angeli (shoulder) out vs. Notre Dame","description":"Syracuse has ruled starting quarterback Steve Angeli out for Saturday's game against Notre Dame due to a shoulder injury.","published":"2026-11-23T18:40:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575118/syracuse-rules-qb-steve-angeli-shoulder-vs-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana not yet naming starting QB for game vs. Purdue, Curt Cignetti says","description":"Indiana is not yet naming a starting quarterback for Saturday's rivalry game against Purdue, coach Curt Cignetti said Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T18:51:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575086/indiana-not-yet-naming-starting-qb-game-vs-purdue","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama's Kalen DeBoer expects QB Keelon Russell to be 'full go' vs. Auburn","description":"Alabama coach Kalen DeBoer said Monday that he expects QB Keelon Russell, who is working his way back from an ankle injury, to be \"full go\" for rivalry week against Auburn.","published":"2026-11-23T18:13:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50574915/alabama-deboer-expects-qb-russell-full-go-auburn","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5136784/francis-brewu","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Francis Brewu","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:30Z","intro":"Francis Brewu (born January 17, 2006) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously played for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In January 2024, Brewu enrolled early at Pittsburgh. He quickly impressed during spring camp due to his size and technique and was moved off of the scout team. He was also named the strongest player on the team by his teammates. Prior to the 2024 season, Brewu was named number 77 on Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List. During the season he played in 12 games with one start and totaled 15 tackles, three tackles for loss and 1.5 sacks. He was also named to the Pro Football Focus (PFF) All-Freshman Team at the end of the season. In December 2024, Brewu announced he would return to the Panthers for 2025. On August 4, 2025, Brewu was again named to Feldman's Freaks List, this time at number 24. In 2025 Brewu started 12 games for the Panthers in which he led all Pitt interior defensive linemen in tackles. Due to his performance, Brewu gained recognition as an Honorable Mention All-ACC selection. On January 6, 2026, Brewu entered the transfer portal, and chose to transfer to the Notre Dame Fighting Irish on January 13. On August 10, 2026, Brewu was named to Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List for the third consecutive season."}]}}